  "description": "Please run the Atropos segmentation on the T1\u2011weighted image located at\u202f/data/patient01_T1.nii.gz, using the associated mask at\u202f/data/patient01_mask.nii.gz. The prior probability images are provided in the directory\u202f/data/prior_probs/, and the final classified output should be written to\u202f/output/patient01_classified.nii.gz.  \n\nThe job will be executed in three dimensions with four parallel threads, segmenting three tissue classes. Initialization will be performed with KMeans, and a random seed will not be used. A Markov random field smoothing factor of\u202f0.2\u202fwill be applied, and the algorithm will stop when the change falls below a convergence threshold of\u202f0.001\u202for after\u202f10\u202fiterations, ignoring prior probabilities below\u202f0.5. The likelihood model is Gaussian. Posterior probability volumes will be saved using the template\u202fPOSTERIOR_%02d.nii.gz. Prior weighting is set to\u202f0.45, and mixture\u2011model proportions are enabled. Verbose output is requested via the \u201c\u2011v\u201d argument. The ICM optimizer will use synchronous updates and may perform up to\u202f5\u202fICM iterations, with a standard posterior formulation."
